card.statement:
\begin{trivlist}

- [(a)] For any $T\in \bigotimes\limits_{s=1}^l {\rm Mat}(n_s)$

\[
(\rho_{n_1, \ldots, n_l}(T))^{\rm{t}}=\rho_{n_l, \ldots, n_1}(\star T).
\]

- [(b)] Let $C_i, D_i\in {\rm Mat}(n_i)$, $i=1,\ldots,l$ such that $C_i$ is similar to $D_i$ for all $i$. Then $\rho_{n_1, \ldots, n_l}(C_1\otimes\ldots \otimes C_l)$ and $\rho_{n_1, \ldots, n_l}(D_1\otimes\ldots \otimes D_l)$ are similar. \end{trivlist}
